**Requirements.** Search buses by source, destination and date; show seat layout and availability; book seats; pay; notify. Non-goal for LLD: global scale.

**Entities.** `Bus` (id, number, type, operator), `Route` (source, destination, distance), `Trip` (id, busId, routeId, departure, arrival, base fare, date), `Seat` (id, busId, number, type), `TripSeat` or `SeatInventory` (tripId, seatId, status AVAILABLE/LOCKED/BOOKED), `Booking` (id, userId, tripId, status, amount), `BookingSeat`, `Payment`, `User`.

**Schema and indexes.** Index `Trip(source, destination, date)` through the route (or denormalise cities onto trip) so search is an index lookup, not a scan. `TripSeat` has a unique key `(tripId, seatId)`.

**Search endpoint (Spring Boot).**
```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/buses")
public class BusController {
  private final BusService service;
  public BusController(BusService service) { this.service = service; }

  @GetMapping("/search")
  public List<TripDto> search(@RequestParam String source,
                              @RequestParam String destination,
                              @RequestParam @DateTimeFormat(iso = ISO.DATE) LocalDate date) {
    return service.searchBus(source, destination, date);
  }
}
```
`@RestController` = controller plus JSON responses; `@RequestMapping`/`@GetMapping` map URLs and methods; `@RequestParam` binds query parameters; `@Service` marks business logic; `@Repository` with Spring Data JPA queries data; `@Entity`, `@Id`, `@ManyToOne` map tables; `@Transactional` wraps booking in a transaction.

**Booking and concurrency.** To avoid double booking, lock seats: update `TripSeat` from AVAILABLE to LOCKED with a compare-and-set (`UPDATE ... WHERE status='AVAILABLE'`) or use optimistic locking (`@Version`). A locked seat has an expiry (for example 10 minutes) and returns to AVAILABLE if payment fails; payment success marks it BOOKED.

**Patterns.** Strategy for `FareStrategy` (base, dynamic, festival pricing), Observer or events for notifications, and a facade `BookingService`. Keep classes small and dependent on interfaces.

**Search performance:** composite index, cache popular routes, paginate and filter by time and bus type.
